 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Doris gave Mr. Plum white tires. By Friday, they were pancakes.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.662
  },
  {
   "text": "Her complaint box said \"black is boring.\" So why are tires black?",
   "s": 3.862,
   "e": 6.774
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Say no more!\" said Doris, and baked tires in pink and mint.",
   "s": 7.074,
   "e": 9.903
  },
  {
   "text": "They looked like cupcakes. Biscuit the dog wanted one as a bed.",
   "s": 10.103,
   "e": 12.756
  },
  {
   "text": "But Route 9 hit 104 degrees, and the pink tires went soft like gum.",
   "s": 12.956,
   "e": 17.06
  },
  {
   "text": "Mrs. Ortiz drove home and left a pink stripe across town.",
   "s": 17.26,
   "e": 20.221
  },
  {
   "text": "Complaint two: \"My tires are melting!\" \"Say no more!\" Doris gave every wheel a tiny umbrella.",
   "s": 20.421,
   "e": 25.201
  },
  {
   "text": "By Saturday, the mint ones popped, and Mr. Plum drove on bare rims, throwing sparks.",
   "s": 25.401,
   "e": 28.647
  },
  {
   "text": "So what's in a boring black tire?",
   "s": 28.847,
   "e": 30.065
  },
  {
   "text": "Soot. Specks of black carbon make rubber many times tougher, like a gummy bear in armor.",
   "s": 30.365,
   "e": 34.67
  },
  {
   "text": "And black blocks the sunshine that cooks rubber. Built-in sunscreen.",
   "s": 34.87,
   "e": 38.239
  },
  {
   "text": "Doris went back to black. Then, one last complaint:",
   "s": 38.639,
   "e": 40.846
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Your dog is sleeping in my spare tire.\" Doris said no more.",
   "s": 40.966,
   "e": 44.184
  }
 ],
